@segment 23-26 Sun Rock, Windshear & Ashenvale (replaces Blackfathom Deeps)
@start-level 23
@carry 1067,529,546,567,98094,742,1195,1068,1095,874,868,1130,3923
@done 1066,1094,1062,3922

# Order: the level 22-25 Stonetalon quests first, then all of Ashenvale, then back to Sun Rock at
# about level 24.7 for the Charred Vale and Gerenzo (mobs 23-27), then the level 26 mage class quest.

# --- On foot from the Crossroads: Malaka'jin and southern Windshear ---
# Your hearthstone is still on cooldown from Tarren Mill. It is ready again long before you next need it.
G The Barrens, 35.3, 27.9 | Run west from the Crossroads along the road to the Stonetalon border, where Seereth Stonebreak stands. 1068 is not finished yet; you come back past him on the way to Ashenvale
A 1058 | Witch Doctor Jin'Zil is in the small cave at Malaka'jin, just past the border into Stonetalon. The parts come from Stonetalon Peak, which you visit soon
A 1090 | Follow the road north into Windshear Crag. Piznik stands at a mine entrance on the east side of the logging camp
C 1090 @ Stonetalon Mountains, 71.9, 60.0 | Piznik mines for about a minute. Stay next to him and kill the Venture Co. patrols that come at him, then talk to him for the ore
T 1090
A 1092
C 1068:1 @ Stonetalon Mountains, 64.1, 46.4 | XT:4 is a goblin shredder (level 23) working the north end of the logging area, by Cragpool Lake. Gerenzo (level 27) stands on the heights just north of it: leave him alone for now
C 1068:2 @ Stonetalon Mountains, 64.1, 56.6 | XT:9, the second shredder (level 23), works the logging area further south
T 1095,1092 | Ziz Fizziks stands under the cliff at the south-west edge of Windshear Crag. He then offers Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle: do not take it yet. You come back for it after Ashenvale, about two levels higher, and leaving it keeps your log small there

# --- Thunder Bluff hop ---
G Stonetalon Mountains, 45.1, 59.8 | Walk west to Sun Rock Retreat and its wind rider master. Take the Sun Rock quests when you come back, not now
FLY Thunder Bluff
T 1067 | Apothecary Zamah is in the Pools of Vision, in the caves under Spirit Rise
A 1086 | Keep the Toxic Fogger. You use it at the goblins' sky port in Windshear Crag near the end of this segment, and hand the quest in to Zamah on a later Thunder Bluff visit
A 97538 @ Thunder Bluff, 54.5, 47.4 | New Forever quest. Tah Winterhoof stands on the central rise. The pods come from Mirkfallon Lake in Stonetalon. Keep the quest: you hand the pods in when you come back to Thunder Bluff early in the next segment (Tah is a few steps from Zangen Stonehoof)
N Buy at least 3 Runes of Teleportation from a reagent vendor before you leave Thunder Bluff. The level 26 class quest uses three Teleports
FLY Sun Rock Retreat

# --- Mirkfallon Lake and Stonetalon Peak (mobs 22-25) ---
A 6301 | Tammra Windfield, in the middle of Sun Rock Retreat
A 1087 | Braelyn Firehand, on the west side of Sun Rock Retreat. Leave the other Sun Rock quests (Charred Vale, mobs up to level 27) until you come back after Ashenvale
C 6301,97538 | Walk north to Mirkfallon Lake. Gaea Seeds lie on the ground around the lake shore. Mirkweed plants grow in the shallow water of the lake; loot 30 Mirkweed Pods from them
C 1087,1058 | Keep going north to Stonetalon Peak (mobs level 22-25). The Sons and Daughters of Cenarius and the Cenarion Botanists camp south of the Alliance outpost at the Peak (stay away from its guards). Sap Beasts (sap), Twilight Runner cats (whiskers), Antlered and Great Coursers (30 eyes, roughly two per deer) and the small Fey Dragons (one scale) all roam the Peak. You do not need the druids and dryads further west (level 25-27)
T 6301 | Walk back south to Sun Rock Retreat. Finish any missing Gaea Seeds or Mirkweed Pods at the lake on the way. Tammra then offers New Life: take it when you come back
T 1087 | Braelyn then offers Ordanus (level 29, up in the druid den on the Peak). Skip it

# --- Back through Windshear to Malaka'jin and the Barrens ---
T 1058 | Walk east into Windshear Crag and follow the road south to Jin'Zil's cave at Malaka'jin
A 6542 | Darn Talongrip, in the Malaka'jin camp beside Jin'Zil's cave. It sends you to Kadrak, who is on your way north
T 1068 | Seereth Stonebreak, just across the border in the Barrens

# --- North through the Barrens into Ashenvale ---
G The Barrens, 48.1, 5.4 | Run north-east across the Dry Hills to Mor'shan Rampart, the Horde gate at the north end of the Barrens
T 6542 | Kadrak, on the Mor'shan watch tower
A 6543 | Kadrak. Right-click the Bundle of Reports for three Warsong Reports. Three Warsong messengers in Ashenvale each take one: talk to each of them, accept his short quest and hand it straight back to get his update
A 6544 | Follow the road north into Ashenvale. Torek and his raiders wait just west of the road, south of Splintertree Post
C 6544 @ Ashenvale, 68.3, 75.3 | Tell Torek you are ready; he charges west into Silverwing Outpost. At the end Duriel Moonfire and four elves jump you inside the building. They have low health: Frost Nova, then burn them down, and drink a potion if needed
A 6503 | Kuray'bin waits by the road a little further north
C 6543:1 @ Ashenvale, 71.0, 68.4 | The Warsong Scout stands next to Kuray'bin: give him the first report
C 6503 | Ashenvale Outrunners are stealthed night elf scouts in the woods on both sides of the road around Kuray'bin and Torek. Walk the slopes; they show themselves when they attack
T 6503
F Splintertree Post
S Splintertree Post | Innkeeper Kaylisk. The class quest later uses this hearth
T 6544 | Ertog Ragetusk
T 742 | Senani Thunderheart
A 6383
T 6383 | This opens the Ashenvale Hunt. Sharptalon (level 31, south of the post) is for much later; skip him
A 25 | Mastok Wrilehiss. Also skip: The Lost Pages (Gurda Ragescar, level 30, the pages are random drops) and Warsong Supplies (needs a crate from Booty Bay and an engineering gun)

# --- West loop: Mystral Lake, Ursangous, Va'xug, Zoram'gar, Thistlefur ---
C 25 | Mystral Lake is south-west of Splintertree. Kill the Befouled Water Elementals around the lake and walk onto the gazebo on the lake (48.9, 69.6) to scout it. Keep away from Silverwind Refuge, the Alliance camp by the lake
A 1918 @ Ashenvale, 45.9, 70.6 | Tideress (level 27) is a named water elemental near the small island in the west of the lake. Her Befouled Water Globe starts this quest
A 23 @ Ashenvale, 39.8, 65.2 | Ursangous (level 25, a druid in bear form) patrols the woods west of Mystral Lake. His paw starts this quest. A huge elite treant also patrols here: keep your distance
A 98251 @ Ashenvale, 40.4, 61.5 | New Forever quest. Va'xug Firefure, a lost warlock, sits in a ravine just north of Ursangous
C 98251 @ Ashenvale, 39.7, 65.4 | Shadowhorn Stags and Ashenvale Bears roam all around the ravine
T 98251 @ Ashenvale, 40.4, 61.5
A 98252 @ Ashenvale, 40.4, 61.5
C 98252 @ Ashenvale, 38.6, 58.3 | Va'xug's Eye of Kilrogg follows you: lead it out of the ravine to the main road within four minutes. If the channel breaks, go back to her and try again
T 98252 @ Ashenvale, 38.6, 58.3 | Hand it in to the Eye of Kilrogg itself, at the road
G Ashenvale, 30.0, 57.0 | Astranaar (Alliance town, level 40 guards) is straight north up this road, only a short way off. Do not follow the road: head due west first, keeping Astranaar well to your right
G Ashenvale, 12.2, 33.8 | Now turn north-west and cross the forest to Zoram'gar Outpost on the coast. Keep clear of the night elves at around 22, 53 (on your left) and of Maestra's Post (Alliance, around 27, 36, on your right)
F Zoram'gar Outpost
C 6543:2 @ Ashenvale, 12.2, 34.2 | The Warsong Runner is in the outpost: give him the second report
A 6442 | Marukai
A 6462 | Mitsuwa
A 216 | Karang Amakkar. Skip Vorsha the Lasher (Muglash) and King of the Foulweald: both are elite
C 6442 | Wrathtail naga line the Zoram Strand north of the outpost. Every kind drops heads
T 6442
C 216 | Thistlefur Village is inland, east of the Zoram Strand. Kill the Avengers and Shamans in and around the village
C 6462 | Thistlefur Hold is the cave at the east end of the village. Troll Chests sit along its tunnels; each holds a Troll Charm
A 6482 | Ruul Snowhoof is a captive tauren deep inside Thistlefur Hold
C 6482 @ Ashenvale, 41.5, 34.5 | Escort Ruul out of the cave. Furbolgs ambush you on the way; keep them off him. Afterwards you only need to talk to his sister in Splintertree. Keep 216 and 6462: you hand them in on a later flight back to Zoram'gar

# --- East across Ashenvale to Splintertree and Night Run ---
A 24 @ Ashenvale, 57.5, 56.0 | Run east-south-east across the middle of Ashenvale. Astranaar (around 36, 50) stays behind you to the south-west, and the worgen (level 29-32, around 50, 39) stay north of your path. Shadumbra (level 28 panther) patrols back and forth just south of Raynewood Retreat; her head starts this quest. Do not go up into Raynewood Retreat (around 62, 51): its guards are elites. Level 40 night elf sentinels guard a moonwell just south-east of her (59, 59): do not pull her toward it
T 6482 | Continue east to Splintertree Post. Yama Snowhoof
T 23,24 | Senani Thunderheart
T 25,1918 | Mastok Wrilehiss
A 824 | The globe goes to Je'neu at Zoram'gar; you fly there before going back to Sun Rock
A 6441 | Pixel
C 6441 @ Ashenvale, 67.5, 54.5 | Night Run is the satyr valley just north-west of Splintertree. Every Felmusk satyr (level 25-27) can drop horns
T 6441 | Pixel
FLY Zoram'gar Outpost
T 824,216,6462 | Je'neu Sancrea, Karang Amakkar and Mitsuwa, all in the outpost

# --- Back to Sun Rock at about 24.7: the Charred Vale, Gerenzo and the sky port ---
FLY Sun Rock Retreat | A long flight with stops on the way
A 6381 | Tammra Windfield, in the middle of Sun Rock Retreat
A 6282,86576 | Maggran Earthbinder gives both. 86576 Bloodfury Trinkets is new in Forever; its sunstones go to Mor'rogal, who stands next to Tsunaman
A 6393 | Tsunaman, on the hill at the south end of Sun Rock Retreat
C 6381,6282,86576,6393 | The Charred Vale is the burnt valley west and south-west of Sun Rock. Plant the seeds in the Gaea Dirt Mounds on the valley floor. Kill all four kinds of Bloodfury harpy: Harpies and Ambushers (level 23-24), Slayers and Roguefeathers (25-26); Glittering Sunstones drop from them. Storm Witches (26-27) hit hard, so pull them one at a time. Incendrites drop from the fire elementals: Rogue Flame Spirits (23-24) on the way in, Burning Ravagers (24-25) and Burning Destroyers (26-27) deeper in the vale; Frost Nova and step back from the Destroyers. Leave Bloodfury Ripper (elite) alone
T 6393 | Back to Sun Rock: Tsunaman, on the south hill
T 86576 @ Stonetalon Mountains, 47.2, 64.0 | Mor'rogal, next to Tsunaman
T 6282 | Maggran then offers Bloodfury Bloodline (elite). Skip it
A 5881 | Maggran's letter goes to Grish Longrunner at the Great Lift in the next segment. Keep it
T 6381 | Tammra Windfield
A 1096 | Walk east to Ziz Fizziks, under the cliff at the south-west edge of Windshear Crag
C 1086 @ Stonetalon Mountains, 66.5, 45.5 | Walk north through Windshear Crag. The sky port is the goblins' landing pad with a parked flying machine, just east of where XT:4 worked: use the Toxic Fogger there, then leave
C 1096 | Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle (level 27) watches the site from high above Cragpool Lake, a little north-west of the pad, next to the big water wheel; follow the path up. Expect to be about level 25, two below him: pull him alone at full mana, open with Frostbolt, Frost Nova when he closes in, step back and keep casting. Loot his Mechanical Arm
T 1096 | Back south to Ziz Fizziks
L 26 @ Stonetalon Mountains, 32.0, 69.0 | Quest XP runs out here. Walk back west past Sun Rock to the south end of the Charred Vale and kill the Bloodfury Slayers, Roguefeathers and Storm Witches and the basilisks there (level 25-28) until level 26. The class quest needs 26

# --- Mage class quest: Nether-lace (level 26) ---
N Teleport: Undercity (uses a Rune of Teleportation). Without the spell, walk to Sun Rock, fly to Orgrimmar and take the zeppelin to Tirisfal Glades instead
A 1943 @ Undercity, 85.1, 10.0 | Anastasia Hartwell in the Magic Quarter
TRAIN | Undercity Magic Quarter: learn your level 24 and 26 spells (Cone of Cold at 26)
N Teleport: Orgrimmar (or take the zeppelin from the tower outside Undercity if you don't have it)
T 1943 | Deino, in the Valley of Spirits
A 1944 | Keep Deino's Flask
T 3923 | Rilli Greasygob, in the Valley of Honor. Skip her next quest, Samophlange Manual: its parts drop from low-level goblins in the northern Barrens
H Splintertree Post
C 6543:3 @ Ashenvale, 81.8, 53.5 | The Warsong Outrider waits on the road east of Splintertree, toward Azshara: give him the last report. Xavian is north-west of him
C 1944 @ Ashenvale, 76.3, 41.5 | Xavian is the satyr ruin north of Splintertree. Use Deino's Flask at the bottom of the highest waterfall, on the west side of the ruins. The satyrs here are level 27-30: pull one at a time or slip past them
N Teleport: Orgrimmar (or fly from Splintertree Post to Orgrimmar if you don't have it)
T 1944 | Deino
A 1945 @ Orgrimmar, 38.5, 86.1 | Deino
FLY Splintertree Post
C 1945 | Laughing Sisters are the dryads in the woods below Raynewood Retreat, west of Splintertree. Kill them for 12 hairs, and loot one Etched Phial (for 1195) from them too. Stay out of Raynewood Retreat itself and away from the guarded moonwell at 59, 59
C 1195 @ Ashenvale, 60.2, 72.9 | Use the Etched Phial at the moonwell on the west bank of the Falfarren River, south of the main road. Keep the Filled Etched Phial for Thunder Bluff in the next segment
G Ashenvale, 69.7, 71.7 | Walk east to the Horde road at the Splintertree guard post, passing north of Silverwing Outpost
T 6543 | Kadrak. Follow the road south out of Ashenvale to Mor'shan Rampart
T 1945 | Kil'hala, the tailor at the Crossroads. Keep following the road south from Mor'shan to the Crossroads
A 1946
T 1946 | Pick the Nether-lace Robe or Tunic
S Crossroads | Bind your hearthstone at the Crossroads inn again
